('acl', 'Spatial/Geometric', 'What set of transformations will transform the leftmost image into the rightmost image?',
 '["A reflection about the line y = x, followed by a translation of 1 unit right and 1 unit up", "A reflection about the line y = x, followed by a translation of 2 units right and 1 unit up", "A translation of 2 units right and 1 unit up, followed by a reflection about the line y = x", "A reflection about the line y = x, followed by a translation of 2 units right and 2 units up"]'::jsonb,
 1, 'Reflecting the shape about the line y = x and then sliding it 2 units right and 1 unit up lands exactly on the pictured result. A reflection does not commute with a translation whose right and up amounts differ, so doing the translation first (or translating by the wrong amount) produces a shape in a different position than the one shown.',
